      "text": "{\"grades\":[{\"id\":\"p1\",\"grade\":\"correct\",\"reason\":\"Correctly identifies prepare_auth special-casing the 2-tuple into HTTPBasicAuth, the __call__ setting Authorization via _basic_auth_str, and the latin1/colon/base64/'Basic ' construction; only trivial details (to_native_string, __dict__ copy, Content-Length recompute) are omitted.\"},{\"id\":\"p2\",\"grade\":\"partly\",\"reason\":\"Gets the body=None part right but explicitly declines to state the key fact that no Content-Length header is set because the method is GET (and that non-GET/HEAD would get '0').\"},{\"id\":\"p3\",\"grade\":\"correct\",\"reason\":\"Names get_encoding_from_headers/_parse_content_type_header, the Content-Type input, utf-8 result, and ISO-8859-1 for text/html without charset.\"},{\"id\":\"p4\",\"grade\":\"correct\",\"reason\":\"Correctly explains that the guess_json_utf branch is skipped because encoding is already set, that text is passed to json.loads, and that a UTF-16 body with encoding='utf-8' would decode to garbage and raise requests.exceptions.JSONDecodeError.\"},{\"id\":\"p5\",\"grade\":\"wrong\",\"reason\":\"Declines to answer, failing to state that select_proxy returned None so path_url was used, and that a configured http proxy would yield urldefragauth(request.url).\"},{\"id\":\"p6\",\"grade\":\"correct\",\"reason\":\"Correctly states CERT_REQUIRED is the scheme-independent default from _urllib3_request_context, CERT_NONE for verify=False, and ca_certs/ca_cert_dir for a path, matching the key despite a small hedge.\"},{\"id\":\"p8\",\"grade\":\"wrong\",\"reason\":\"Says the documentation doesn't cover it rather than stating that the 3-tuple falls to the callable branch and raises TypeError: 'tuple' object is not callable.\"},{\"id\":\"g1\",\"grade\":\"wrong\",\"reason\":\"Denies the once-only contract and misses both the cookielib has_header mechanism and the fact that resolve_redirects pops the 'Cookie' header before re-preparing.\"},{\"id\":\"g2\",\"grade\":\"correct\",\"reason\":\"Describes the ordered prefix matching (longest/first match), mount, InvalidSchema on no match, and the look-alike-host misuse invited by plain string prefix matching.\"},{\"id\":\"g3\",\"grade\":\"correct\",\"reason\":\"Correctly identifies should_strip_auth stripping on host (and port) change and the deliberately allowed http→https default-port upgrade; only omits the changed_scheme nuance.\"},{\"id\":\"g4\",\"grade\":\"correct\",\"reason\":\"Matches the key: trust_env gating, explicit verify wins over env, REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE preferred over CURL_CA_BUNDLE, and the prepared-request/send caveat requiring merge_environment_settings.\"},{\"id\":\"g5\",\"grade\":\"correct\",\"reason\":\"States the default DEFAULT_RETRIES=0 (no retries) versus three connection retries with max_retries=3, plus the Retry object option and RetryError, though it omits the read=False nuance of the default.\"},{\"id\":\"g6\",\"grade\":\"partly\",\"reason\":\"Correctly explains chunked is used for length-less iterables via super_len in prepare_body, but fails to give the adapter's actual decision rule (chunked = body is not None and no Content-Length header).\"},{\"id\":\"g7\",\"grade\":\"partly\",\"reason\":\"Gives the correct general guarantee and several mappings (ConnectTimeout, ReadTimeout, SSLError, ConnectionError) but omits/hedges on the MaxRetryError reason inspection, ProtocolError/OSError, ClosedPoolError, InvalidHeader, and LocationValueError→InvalidURL.\"}]}",
